/E (ABSTRACT )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
129 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 103 0 R
/E (Thisassignment proposes an integrated ethical-hacking engagement framework for a university preparing to assess its student portal, learning-management system \(LMS\), email service and campus network. The initial programme covers approximately 20 systems and 50 staff members and is designed to expand across the university, including approved third-party assessors. The framework combines written authorization, asset-based scope control, legal compliance, hacker threat classification, ethical rules, an isolated virtual lab, reusable documents, coordinated vulnerability disclosure and governance evaluation. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
130 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 103 0 R
/E (The central principle is that technical permission alone is not enough. Every activity must be authorized by the correct owner, remain within a written scope, follow applicable law, protect personal information and avoid unnecessary harm. All examples and measurements are academic design simulations. No live university system is scanned, accessed or exploited. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
