/Title (This assignment designed an integrated ethical-hacking engagement framework for a university programme. It covers enquiry and blueprint, hacker classification, ethics, legal compliance, rules of engagement, authorization, coordinated disclosure, isolated lab, reusable documents, integration testing, scalability and changed requirements.)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 795 0 R
/Next 923 0 R
>>
endobj
923 0 obj
<<
/Title (The key learning is that ethical hacking is defined not only by technical skill but also by permission, boundaries, accountability and responsible communication. Written authorization identifies who can test which assets, when and by what methods. Legal and privacy controls protect the university and the people whose information is stored in its systems. The isolated lab provides a safe place for practical learning, while reusable documents and a central register make the process repeatable.)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 795 0 R
/Prev 922 0 R
>>
endobj
